  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 7902.03 Definitions",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 7902.03 Definitions.\n\n(a) “Caregiver\" means “caregiver” as defined by RSA 106-J:3, I.\n\n(b) \"Department\" means “department” as defined by RSA 106-J:3, II.\n\n(c) “Designated media outlet” means a participating radio station, television station, or other local, regional, or statewide media outlet that has been designated by a local law enforcement agency or the department to receive alert bulletins regarding missing persons in the state.\n\n(d) “Division” means the division of state police.\n\n(e) “Law enforcement agency” means “law enforcement agency” as defined by RSA 105-D:1, V.\n\n(f) “Media” means “media” as defined in RSA 106-M:1, V.\n\n(g) “Medic Alert + Safe Return program” means a program that helps identify and locate wandering or lost missing persons with Alzheimer’s or related dementia and return them home.\n\n(h) \"Missing vulnerable adult\" means “missing vulnerable adult” as defined by RSA 106-J:3, III.\n\nSource. #14199, eff 2-25-25",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c7900.html"
